@@ -67,6 +67,14 @@ ## User Administration
 
 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue management
+
+Queues are created, renamed and deactivated by entity owners/admins only (`App\Actions\CreateQueue`, `App\Actions\UpdateQueue`). Names are trimmed (1-255 chars); slugs are unique within an entity and default to `Str::slug(name)`. Deactivation (`is_active = false`) retires a queue without deleting it; issuing or calling on an inactive queue raises `InactiveQueueException`.
+
+### Queue access
+
+Per-queue permissions are granted by owners/admins via `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess`: a non-empty permission list upserts a `queue_access` row for a membership, an empty list revokes it. The only permission today is `call` (`App\Enums\QueuePermission::Call`). Owners/admins may always call; employees need a `queue_access` row whose `permissions` contains `call`. Grants/revokes are recorded on the `audit` log channel (`queue.access.granted` / `queue.access.revoked`).
+
 ### Ticket
 
 Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (filled when called). Attributes:
